## Layer 2: Atomic Update & Reset Transaction

### Scope Contract
Execute the definitive transaction that purges the product's legacy/corrupted IDs (e.g., `6vL2...`) and records the verified semantic array using the `--commit` flag.

### DoD

- [ ] 2.1 — In `scripts/product-vfs-mapper/index.mjs`: Finalize `resetAndPopulateCatalogueKeys(productId, determinedIds)` using a Sanity transaction.
  - Sequence: `patch(productId).unset(['catalogueLocationKeys']).set({ catalogueLocationKeys: determinedIds })`.
  - Difficulty: 2 - A(scripts/product-vfs-mapper/index.mjs): implement atomic unset/set logic

- [ ] 2.2 — Finalize CLI argument handling to support the `--commit` flag vs `--dry-run`.
  - Difficulty: 1 - C(scripts/product-vfs-mapper/index.mjs): finalize CLI controls

### Verification — Layer 2

- [ ] V2.1 — Execute the script with `--commit` on the target product ID.
- [ ] V2.2 — Query `*[_id == "Y7l1IhzX2fnyiano4ius6H"][0].catalogueLocationKeys` via CLI or Vision and confirm it strictly contains the 2 correct IDs.
  - Difficulty: 1

