## Layer 3: Hardened VFS GROQ Verification

### Scope Contract
Fix the `param $leafId referenced, but not provided` and syntax errors in `verify-mapping.mjs`. Implement proper array-intersection GROQ and decoupled Sub-Tree logic.

### DoD

- [ ] 3.1 — In `scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs`: Fix **Positive Leaf Test**. Use the valid Sanity array-membership syntax: `*[_type == "product" && $leafId in catalogueLocationKeys]{name}`.
  - Difficulty: 2 - B(scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs): fix leaf membership query

- [ ] 3.2 — In `scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs`: Fix **Positive Header (Sub-Tree) Test**. Implement `getSubTreeLeafIds(headerId)` in-memory by recursively walking the catalogue hierarchy.
  - Evaluate intersection: `*[_type == "product" && count(catalogueLocationKeys[@ in $subTreeIds]) > 0]{name}`.
  - Difficulty: 5 - A(scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs): implement recursive sub-tree ID collector

- [ ] 3.3 — Fix **Negative Co-Branch Test**. Use the same `$leafId in catalogueLocationKeys` syntax to assert the product does NOT match contradictory siblings.
  - Difficulty: 1 - B(scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs): fix negative branch checks

- [ ] 3.4 — Implement dynamic leaf querying to prevent `Cannot read properties of null` when testing stale IDs.
  - Difficulty: 2 - E(scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs): add defensive null checks

### Verification — Layer 3

- [ ] V3.1 — Run `node scripts/product-vfs-mapper/verify-mapping.mjs --productId="Y7l1IhzX2fnyiano4ius6H"`.
- [ ] V3.2 — Confirm matching 100% PASS for Positive Leaf, Positive Header, and Negative Co-Branch tests.
  - Difficulty: 1

